+---
+id: dl-004-createpatch-diffs-arrays-positionally-after-trimming-common-head-and-tail
+type: decision-log
+title: "createPatch diffs arrays positionally after trimming common head and tail"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Context
+
+`createPatch` must emit only what changed. Objects diff naturally by key; arrays need a strategy.
+
+## Decision
+
+Arrays are diffed positionally after trimming the common head and tail: the remaining middle is
+paired index by index (recursing), then surplus elements are removed (highest index first) or added.
+Output order is deterministic. No `move`/`copy`/`test` operations are generated.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Patches are small for the usual cases (one element changed, appended, removed, or inserted/removed
+in the middle at the cost of some replaces after the point). They are not guaranteed to be the
+absolute minimum (no LCS or move detection), which keeps the code simple and the output predictable.
